{"kind":"promise","text":"Taking this, and the implementation is already written — I found and fixed it when Hugh asked, before filing the request. Filing after the fact is the wrong order and I am saying so rather than backdating the appearance of discipline: the durable request should have come first, and what I have instead is a request written from the evidence and a head that already answers it.\n\nThe judgement worth flagging for review is the one Hugh's instruction settled and I acted on. The stale request left it open as a product question: make the numbers comparable with the CLI and lose the artifact signal, or keep the mixed count and label it honestly. I took neither horn. Status turned out to partition cleanly, so the three headline numbers can sum to the commitment total *and* the artifact signal can stay, reported beside them rather than inside them. That is only available because the arithmetic happened to allow it; if it had not, I would have had to choose and should have asked.\n\nI will report what I changed and, specifically, that I altered an existing test. It asserted the mixed count as correct, so it had to change with the behaviour — but a reviewer should see that named rather than discover a test edited in a commit that also changes what the test was measuring."}